Molecular O-Zone Consomme with Deconstructed Citrus Reduction.

An avant-garde, hyper-reductive modernist broth designed to express the singular, circular essence of the letter O through unnecessary culinary and computational complexity.

Ingredients.
5 star anise
3 whole cloves
4 green cardamom pods
4 black peppercorns
12 juniper berries
3 cinnamon sticks
1 pinch saffron threads
7 g coriander seeds
9 g coarse sea salt
100 ml filtered water

Cooking time: 45 minutes.
Pre-heat oven to 180 degrees Celsius.

Method.
Put star anise into the 1st mixing bowl.
Combine whole cloves into the 1st mixing bowl.
Put green cardamom pods into the 2nd mixing bowl.
Chop the green cardamom pods.
Add black peppercorns into the 1st mixing bowl.
Chop the green cardamom pods until chopped.
Combine whole cloves into the 1st mixing bowl.
Remove star anise from the 1st mixing bowl.
Put saffron threads into the 3rd mixing bowl.
Add coriander seeds into the 3rd mixing bowl.
Add coarse sea salt into the 3rd mixing bowl.
Stir the 3rd mixing bowl for 2 minutes.
Fold coarse sea salt into the 3rd mixing bowl.
Put juniper berries into the 4th mixing bowl.
Combine cinnamon sticks into the 4th mixing bowl.
Fold coarse sea salt into the 4th mixing bowl.
Serve with Deconstructed Citrus Reduction.
Add coarse sea salt into the 1st mixing bowl.
Remove coarse sea salt from the 1st mixing bowl.
Liquefy contents of the 1st mixing bowl.
Pour contents of the 1st mixing bowl into the baking dish.
Refrigerate for 1 hours.

Serves 1.

Deconstructed Citrus Reduction.

A tart, hyper-reduced sub-recipe that computes twenty-seven and hands it back to the head chef.

Ingredients.
3 Meyer lemons
2 blood oranges
2 key limes

Method.
Put Meyer lemons into the 1st mixing bowl.
Combine Meyer lemons into the 1st mixing bowl.
Combine Meyer lemons into the 1st mixing bowl.
Add blood oranges into the 1st mixing bowl.
Remove key limes from the 1st mixing bowl.
Liquefy Meyer lemons.